<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Stoddart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1806–1842</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Stoddart was a British army officer sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> in 1838 to reassure <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> Nasrullah about British aims in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and to seek the release of Russian captives. Accused of slighting the emir, he was thrown into a vermin-infested pit and held for years. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-conolly">Arthur Conolly</a> arrived to secure his release, both were beheaded before the Ark citadel in June 1842.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-stoddart.jpg" alt="Charles Stoddart" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Brockedon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_Stoddart.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
